<title>GERMANY: Mannesmann says EU approves Vallourec tie.</title>
<headline>Mannesmann says EU approves Vallourec tie.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission has approved the tubes cooperation between Mannesmann Roehren Werke and France's Vallourec, parent company Mannesmann AG said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The agreement, which would make Mannesmann the largest shareholder in France's biggest steel maker effective October 1, has also been approved by the supervisory boards of both companies, and now needs only the approval of Vallourec's annual general meeting, Mannesmann said.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
